meta {
  name: Manually retry the failed job (API equivalent of Cockpit "Increment retries")
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

put {
  url: {{engineRest}}/job/{{failedJobId}}/retries
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "retries": 3
  }
}

docs {
  # Manual retry

  This re-arms the failed order job with fresh retries — exactly what the Cockpit
  "Increment retries" button does. Because BIKE-FAIL is a *permanent* simulated
  outage, the job will run, fail again, and the incident returns once the retries
  are exhausted. That is the teaching point: a manual retry re-runs the work but is
  not a fix for a systematic error. To demonstrate an actual fix, start a fresh
  request with a valid bike id (e.g. BIKE-900) and watch it complete.
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}
